cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "SPEDLex: a cited, privacy-graded safelist of U.S. special-education terms"
message: "If you use SPEDLex, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
authors:
  - name: "Jeremy Evans"
  - name: "SPEDLex contributors"
version: "0.45.0"
date-released: "2026-10-09"
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/SiskinSkai/spedlex"
url: "https://SiskinSkai.github.io/spedlex/"
abstract: >-
  An open vocabulary that helps de-identification tools remove a child's
  personal information from special-education documents without destroying
  their meaning, so caregivers can use AI tools safely. A concept-oriented
  vocabulary of U.S. special-education terms drawn from
  the IDEA Part B regulations and state special-education documents. Each
  concept carries its surface forms, citations to the documents that attest
  it, and a privacy-risk grade that tells de-identification tools when the
  term can be protected from redaction without sheltering personal names.
keywords:
  - special education
  - IEP
  - IDEA
  - de-identification
  - controlled vocabulary
  - safelist
